  "id": "COMPOUND:42309 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a strong, indirect relationship between 2-Hydroxy-3-Formyl-7-Methoxycarbazole and Carboxylesterase 2, with the target entity Raji acting as a mediator. This compound is consistently identified as a target of Raji, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and a related metabolite. These compounds are all implicated in the targeting of Carboxylesterase 2, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the enzyme. The evidence suggests that 2-Hydroxy-3-Formyl-7-Methoxycarbazole may interact with Raji, which then targets Carboxylesterase 2 through a complex pathway involving multiple molecular interactions. The consistent presence of Raji as a target across different compounds supports the idea that this compound may play a role in the regulation or inhibition of Carboxylesterase 2, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
